## What

Thin adapter crate wrapping `pkix-zlint-bridge` (PKIX-jy95.7) findings as workspace `Lint` impls.

Per PKIX-jy95.1 decision (A2: per-check, runtime-enumerated): the adapter creates ~700 dynamic `Lint` instances, one per zlint check the bridge enumerates. Each Lint carries `(check_id: &'static str, bridge: Arc<ZlintBridge>)` and reads from the bridge's per-cert result cache.

## Shape

```rust
pub struct ZlintLint {
    info: ZlintLintInfo,         // from pkix_zlint_bridge::enumerate_lints()
    bridge: Arc<ZlintBridge>,
}

impl Lint for ZlintLint {
    fn id(&self) -> &str { self.info.check_id }
    fn citation(&self) -> &str { /* from info */ }
    fn check(&self, cert: &Certificate, ctx: &LintContext) -> LintResult {
        // call bridge.run_on_cert(cert) — cached per cert across all ~700 Lint reads
        // look up self.info.check_id in the returned per-check verdicts
        // translate Verdict → LintResult per .2 severity mapping decision (already in bridge)
    }
    // ... applies_to, etc.
}

pub fn all_lints(bridge: Arc<ZlintBridge>) -> Vec<Box<dyn Lint>> {
    bridge.enumerate_lints()
        .into_iter()
        .map(|info| Box::new(ZlintLint { info, bridge: bridge.clone() }) as Box<dyn Lint>)
        .collect()
}
```

## Acceptance

- [ ] `pkix-policy-zlint` crate added to workspace
- [ ] One `Lint` per zlint check (~700)
- [ ] Per-cert subprocess cost amortized via bridge cache
- [ ] Round-trip test against zlint's own `testdata/` (Apache-2.0; cite zlint upstream)
- [ ] CHANGELOG entry
- [ ] AGENTS.md updated to mention `pkix-policy-zlint` ships

## Out of scope

- Bridge crate implementation (PKIX-jy95.7)
- Umbrella-per-profile-family option (rejected in PKIX-jy95.1)

## Blocks on

- PKIX-jy95.7 — pkix-zlint-bridge ships first
- PKIX-jy95.8 — only for pattern parity check; not a strict dep

## Cross-references

- PKIX-jy95 (parent, closed after .10/.11 filed per .9 closure cascade)
- PKIX-jy95.1 (lint granularity = A2 per-check)
- PKIX-jy95.2 (severity mapping = decided at bridge layer)
- PKIX-jy95.6 (two-layer adapter pattern)
- AGENTS.md non-negotiable #5 (industry-forum policy via adapter crates)
- AGENTS.md non-negotiable #6 (cache-friendliness — bridge owns the per-cert cache)
